  "diagnosis": "The dmft_subspace_model_window error (25.0 meV vs 20 meV threshold) indicates the Wannier model does not reproduce the target Mn 3d + O 2p manifold faithfully enough up to 2 eV above E_F. The frontier's parameter sweep shows a clear monotonic improvement as dis_proj_max is lowered: 0.95\u2192208 meV, 0.9\u219237.6 meV, 0.85\u219224.9 meV. The best frontier runs (4 and 8) used dis_proj_max=0.85 with dis_proj_min=0.02. My attempt 1 used dis_proj_min=0.005 and got 25.0 meV, confirming dis_proj_min=0.02 is slightly better. The pao_subset (Mn d1, O p1) already matches the target orbitals exactly, so projectability measures alignment with the correct subspace. Lowering dis_proj_max further freezes more states that project well onto the target orbitals, constraining the disentanglement to reproduce them exactly. The construction converges well and centres are correct; the only gap is fidelity in the target window. dis_froz_max cannot help because the energy window up to +2 eV holds >8 states at some k-points (max fitting e_max is -0.54 eV). num_bands is fixed at 48 by the parent's band count.",
